    {"claim": "A ban without enforcement backbone is a press release with a statutory citation: UK age-verification for porn collapsed due to VPN circumvention with compliance below 40%, social media bans drove teens to encrypted apps.", "targets": [], "relationship": "main"},
    {"claim": "The ban must include binding enforcement mandates, anti-circumvention testing funded at the FTC, and grants to community youth mental health services to avoid prohibitionist backfire.", "targets": [], "relationship": "supporting"},
    {"claim": "The 'explicitly marketed' threshold is a loophole: teenagers jailbreak general-purpose assistants into romantic roles, and the distinction is an advertising claim, not a functional reality.", "targets": [], "relationship": "main"},
    {"claim": "Smart toys with always-on mics and cameras (VTech breach of 6.4 million children, CloudPets unsecured voice messages) perform companion-like surveillance without the label, evading the ban entirely.", "targets": [], "relationship": "supporting"},
    {"claim": "Federal preemption must be a floor, not a ceiling; the statute must preserve state authority and fund state-level enforcement to prevent industry capture.", "targets": [], "relationship": "main"},
    {"claim": "The ban as drafted does nothing to audit sensor-laden toys already in children's bedrooms—that's a structural gap that renders the law performative.", "targets": [], "relationship": "supporting"}
  ]
